{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/988715-familiar-2e-sheet","id":988715,"title":"Familiar 2E Sheet","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-16T23:40:22-07:00","id":988715,"title":"Familiar 2E Sheet","content":"So my players start to play with 2E mechanics and, as always, they want to get their own Familiar. As mage own 2E has been taken off the Familiar section, I propose to design proper sheet for them. Before reinventing the wheel, first look on to <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/NWOD/CofD_EphemeralBeings_1-Page_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">CoD Ephemeral Entity sheet</a>. From my POV, we only need to add second page to this on physical animals stats that Familiar is taking Fetter or Possession with. Any one have idea what could be needed also on this second page for Familiars specifically?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T01:09:32-07:00","id":988730,"title":"","content":"You do know that they don't have to be physically embodied right?<br /> <br /> No there isn't anything you need besides that though. Being a familiar doesn't change an entity much.<br /> <br /> Assuming the right Manifestations or magic there's no reason a familiar is limited to being embodied in animals by the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 10-17-2016, 04:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T03:02:02-07:00","id":988756,"title":"","content":"Well, that's why I think about whole animal part as 2nd page of sheet - it's stereotypical choosing, but everyone can get without them. I mean, let say I have Familiar locked in cat or toad - it works as it have stats of cat when attacking or have Initiative of toad instead of spirit? Maybe higher of those two?<br /> <br /> One way or another, stats for 'physical' part of the Familiar is good to have, just in case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T03:42:24-07:00","id":988769,"title":"","content":"It depends on the manifestation the familiar is using. If the familiar is only fettered to an animal then you technically have a pet with a separate entity attached to it. The familiar could direct your pet to attack but that would be your familiar's action and the pet's action. The pet might attack on its own, in which case the familiar would still have an action available to deliver it's own attack or do something else.<br /> <br /> If the familiar is possessing the pet then they're basically one and the same entity and you'd use the pet's physical stats to determine thing like Initiative or attacking or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}